        "transcriptHtml": "<p class=\"transcript-note\">Automatic transcript. It may contain small recognition errors; the answer key is authoritative.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[11:38]</span> Section three. You are going to hear a conversation between Sally and Ben. They are new college students. You now have some time to read questions twenty-one to twenty-five.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[12:13]</span> Now, listen to the first part of the conversation and answer questions. Questions twenty-one to twenty-five. Hi, Ben. Sally.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[12:43]</span> How are you? Fine. I wanted you to find Ron into you. When did you get here?</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[12:50]</span> I only arrived last night, just in time. I prefer to travel on Sundays to miss the working rush. I suppose you arrived in plenty of time. Oh, I&#x27;ve been here for four days now, so it must have been Thursday that I arrived.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[13:05]</span> I&#x27;d like to have a good chance to look around and settle in. I should have come earlier too. I&#x27;m hoping to get a part-time job. Well, you&#x27;ve no time today, I suppose.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[13:15]</span> Do you still plan to be an architect? Yes. It&#x27;s what I&#x27;ve always wanted to do. And you were planning to do economics, weren&#x27;t you?</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[13:24]</span> Yes, I was. But I&#x27;ve decided on psychology instead. How many textbooks do you have to get? I&#x27;ve been given this long list and I&#x27;m sure they&#x27;ll cost a fortune.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[13:34]</span> See? That looks a lot. It&#x27;s longer than my list. Well, it&#x27;s fourteen, all told.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[13:43]</span> So I might use library copies instead of buying some of them. What about you? I&#x27;ll probably buy the whole lot of mine because I only have five on my list. Although I&#x27;m sure there are many more I&#x27;ll have to read.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[13:56]</span> Luckily, we don&#x27;t have to read them all straight away. Have you got your class timetable yet? It came with the book list. And do you all like to start?</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[14:05]</span> Tuesday. That&#x27;s tomorrow. How about yours? Oh, I&#x27;ve got an extra day, the day after you all start.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[14:13]</span> Now you have some time to read questions 26 to 30. As the conversation continues, they are talking about their new college life. Listen carefully and answer questions 26 to 30. It&#x27;s nothing like school, is it?</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[14:49]</span> Not so far. And the lectures will certainly be different. Do you have any special approach for keeping up with lectures and the amount we have to read? Well, they usually try to read every word in a book.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[15:01]</span> In case I missed something important. So I suppose I&#x27;ll try to write down every word of the lecture if I can. Oh, I couldn&#x27;t do that. I&#x27;d get cramp in my fingers and I wouldn&#x27;t really hear what was being said.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[15:15]</span> I usually skim a book when I read and underline key parts. So I guess I&#x27;ll try to make notes on the main points of the lecture. Have you thought of using a cassette recorder? You mean to record the lecture?</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[15:28]</span> Yep. Then you could make really good notes. Is it allowed? I think so.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[15:34]</span> It must be. Plenty of people seem to do it. It has to be better than trying to write every word as you listen. Anyway, what&#x27;s your first lecture about?</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[15:44]</span> Oh, it&#x27;s on the Industrial Revolution. The Industrial Revolution sounds boring to me. Not really. It made a big difference to everything, including architecture eventually.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[15:55]</span> So what&#x27;s your first lecture about? It&#x27;s about what separates humans from other animals. Okay. Look, I was on my way to the library to check out some of these books on my list.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[16:06]</span> I have a tutorial paper to give in a couple of weeks. Oh, what&#x27;s the topic? Well, I think our lecturer must have trouble thinking up topics. The topic is...</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[16:17]</span> Why study architecture? I don&#x27;t know. It could give you a chance to set out what you want to do. I guess so.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[16:26]</span> Have you been given any tutorials to do yet? Yes. Mine is called... Needs for sleep.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[16:33]</span> Sounds almost as interesting as mine. This is the end of section three. You now have half a minute to check your answers.</p>"
